Here is an example of a custom MySQL function that calculates the average age of users based on their birth year and a specific condition:
```
DELIMITER //
CREATE FUNCTION calculate_avg_age(condition_value INT) RETURNS DECIMAL(10,2)
BEGIN
    DECLARE total_age DECIMAL(10,2);
    DECLARE total_users INT;
    DECLARE avg_age DECIMAL(10,2);

    SELECT SUM(YEAR(CURDATE()) - birth_year) INTO total_age, COUNT(*) INTO total_users
    FROM users
    WHERE condition = condition_value;

    SET avg_age = total_age / total_users;

    RETURN avg_age;
END //
DELIMITER ;
```
This function takes in a parameter `condition_value` which is the value of the specific condition that needs to be met. It then calculates the total age of all users that meet the condition and divides it by the total number of users that meet the condition to get the average age. Finally, it returns the average age as a decimal value. 
To use this function, you can simply call it in a MySQL query like this:
```
SELECT calculate_avg_age(1) AS avg_age FROM users;
```
This will return the average age of all users in the `users` table that have a `condition` value of 1.

