1. Tokenization: Split the input sentence into individual words or tokens.
2. Part-of-speech (POS) tagging: Assign a part of speech tag to each token (e.g. noun, verb, adjective, etc.).
3. Dependency parsing: Identify the relationships between the tokens in the sentence.
4. Sentiment analysis: Determine the overall sentiment of the sentence (positive, negative, or neutral).
5. Apply the intensifiers: Identify the appropriate intensifiers based on the context and sentiment of the sentence, and add them to the appropriate adjectives in the sentence.
Here's an example C# code that demonstrates how to integrate the function into an NLP pipeline:
```
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;
// Define the intensifiers and inappropriate words
string[] intensifiers = { "very", "extremely", "incredibly", "highly", "really", "so", "super" };
string[] inappropriate = { "damn", "effing", "freaking", "fricking", "hella", "mad", "mega", "wicked" };
// Define a function to filter out inappropriate intensifiers
List<string> FilterIntensifiers(List<string> intensifiers, List<string> inappropriate)
{
    return intensifiers.Except(inappropriate).ToList();
}
