Can you solve this puzzle? You are given a binary tree represented by a class with the following structure:
class Node {
    public int val;
    public Node left;
    public Node right;
    public Node(int val=0, Node left=null, Node right=null) {
        this.val = val;
        this.left = left;
        this.right = right;
    }
}
Your task is to find the first common ancestor of two nodes. But wait, there's a twist! Your algorithm must have a time complexity of O(n). Can you figure out how to solve this puzzle with the added requirement?
Provide the C# code for your algorithm. If there is no common ancestor, return null. Good luck!

output:
Yes, I can help you with that. Here's the C# code for finding the first common ancestor of two nodes in a binary tree with a time complexity of O(n):
```
class Solution {
    public Node FindLCA(Node root, Node p, Node q) {
        if (root == null) return null;
        if (root == p || root == q) return root;

        Node left = FindLCA(root.left, p, q);
        Node right = FindLCA(root.right, p, q);

        if (left != null && right != null) return root;
        return left != null ? left : right;
    }
}
```
In this code, we recursively traverse the binary tree and check if the current node is either of the two nodes we are looking for. If it is, we return the node. If not, we recursively search for the two nodes in the left and right subtrees of the current node. If we find both nodes in different subtrees, we return the current node as the first common ancestor. If we find only one node, we continue searching for the other node. If we don't find any node, we return null.

