What is the Go code to calculate the day of the week for a given date in the format of "MM/DD/YYYY" using Zeller's congruence algorithm?
Here is the Go code that uses Zeller's congruence algorithm:
func dayOfWeek(month int, day int, year int) string {
    daysOfWeek := []string{"Saturday", "Sunday", "Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday"}
    if month < 3 {
        month += 12
        year--
    }
    var q = day
    var m = month
    var k = year % 100
    var j = year / 100
    var h = (q + 13*(m+1)/5 + k + k/4 + j/4 - 2*j) % 7
    return daysOfWeek[h]
}
To use this code, simply call the dayOfWeek function and pass in the month, day, and year as parameters in the format of "MM/DD/YYYY". The function will return the corresponding day of the week as a string.

